        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 54.86,
          "en": "soon we will add a custom button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.86,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "But for the moment we can add to the built-in button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 61.55,
          "en": "and give it a title of Take Image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.55,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "and then add the onPress prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 67.86,
          "en": "and in our component function at a handler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.86,
          "end": 70.53,
          "en": "the takeImageHandler for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.53,
          "end": 73.69,
          "en": "that should be executed when that button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.69,
          "end": 77.083,
          "en": "So that's the function we pass as a value for onPress.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.06,
          "end": 80.2,
          "en": "Now in this View we'll show the preview,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.2,
          "end": 81.51,
          "en": "but for the moment we'll not worry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.51,
          "end": 83.63,
          "en": "about that we'll do this in a second step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.63,
          "end": 85.24,
          "en": "for the moment I just wanna to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.24,
          "end": 88.973,
          "en": "that we do open the camera with the takeImageHandler here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.83,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "And how can we now do this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 95.34,
          "en": "Well, with help of this package we just installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.34,
          "end": 98.68,
          "en": "From there, we can import various things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.68,
          "end": 103.33,
          "en": "So from expo-image-picker, and we can for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.33,
          "end": 107.57,
          "en": "import the launchCameraAsync,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.57,
          "end": 109.72999999999999,
          "en": "which will launch the device camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.72999999999999,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "and wait for us to take an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 114.97,
          "en": "Now we can execute this imported function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.97,
          "end": 117.94,
          "en": "here in takeImageHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.94,
          "end": 120.88,
          "en": "There, we can execute it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.88,
          "end": 123.86,
          "en": "but as the name async already suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.86,
          "end": 126.23,
          "en": "this will return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.23,
          "end": 129.43,
          "en": "because of course it doesn't finish immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.43,
          "end": 133.92,
          "en": "instead it waits for the user to press the camera button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "to take a photo and this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "therefore won't finish execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 140.1,
          "en": "before that photo was taken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 142.583,
          "en": "So it will wait for the user to take a photo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 145.49,
          "en": "Hence we wanna wait for this as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.49,
          "end": 147.49,
          "en": "before we try to work with that photo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.49,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "because the photo only exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 153.44,
          "en": "after this function have finished execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.44,
          "end": 156.2,
          "en": "And hence we can convert our takeImageHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.2,
          "end": 158.99,
          "en": "into a async function so that we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.99,
          "end": 161.26,
          "en": "the await keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.26,
          "end": 164.463,
          "en": "And then we'll get this image once this is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.38,
          "end": 168.61,
          "en": "Now we will see what exactly this image is soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.61,
          "end": 170.32999999999998,
          "en": "for the moment we can simply log it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.32999999999998,
          "end": 173.113,
          "en": "to the console here to see it as soon as we have it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.95,
          "end": 176.32999999999998,
          "en": "But before we can see anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.32999999999998,
          "end": 179.69299999999998,
          "en": "I wanna configure my camera a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.55,
          "end": 183.1,
          "en": "For this we can pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.1,
          "end": 187.01,
          "en": "to launchCameraAsync, and of course that is also something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.01,
          "end": 189.56,
          "en": "you learn in the official docs of this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.56,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "There you find the launchCameraAsync function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 196.91,
          "en": "and you learn that you can pass some options to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.91,
          "end": 201.273,
          "en": "and you can then click here to which options can be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.67000000000002,
          "end": 205.62,
          "en": "So it's this list of option that we could set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.62,
          "end": 209.82,
          "en": "for this launchCameraAsync function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 213.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now in my case here, I wanna set some of these options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.57999999999998,
          "end": 216.81,
          "en": "For example, I'll set allowsEditing to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.81,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "to the allow the user to edit the photo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 221.31,
          "en": "before confirming it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.31,
          "end": 224.84,
          "en": "I will set the aspect ratio to an array of two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.84,
          "end": 229.71,
          "en": "which is 16,9 in my case, and I'll set the quality to 0.5",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.75,
          "end": 233.92000000000002,
          "en": "to make sure that we don't get super large images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
